Changes to sing-box v1.14.4 (GNU GPL v3.0 or later), made by the unbraid authors, last on 2026-11-18:
a route chosen by a rule's own destination ip_cidr (or ip_is_private) dials only the resolved addresses that rule
covers. Before, the rule matched when any one address of a name's answer was covered, and its outbound got the whole
list: one local address in an answer took the name's public addresses out on the local route ("Local network bypasses
the VPN", the home tunnels) too. A rule that matched otherwise (a domain item, a rule set, an inverted rule, a DNS
answer) keeps every address.
Applied by tools/build-libbox.sh; git apply skips these lines.

